<b>Madonna - Ray Of Light: Instrumentals (1998) | AAC 256kbps / 48kHz </b><br>
<br>
<i><b>Ray of Light</b></i> is the seventh studio album by American singer and songwriter <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Madonna</a>. It was released on February 22, 1998, by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Maverick Records</a>. A major stylistic and aesthetic departure from her previous works, <i>Ray of Light</i> reflected the singer's embrace of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabbalah" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Kabbalah</a>, study of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hinduism" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Hinduism</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddhism" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Buddhism</a>, and daily practice of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashtanga_vinyasa_yoga" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Ashtanga yoga</a>.<br>
